> Module Savers_credit

> Using Types
> Using Params_2024 as P
> Using Rounding as R

# Retirement savings contributions credit (the Saver's credit): Form 8880

Direct File module `saversCredits.xml` ("DF" below,
`../direct-file/direct-file/backend/src/main/resources/tax/saversCredits.xml`,
1,705 lines). Issue #29, scope.md section 6.4. Law: 26 U.S.C. § 25B
(`sources/statute/irc-25B.html`), Notice 2023-75 section 3
(`sources/revproc/n-23-75.pdf` p 3), Form 8880 (2024)
(`sources/forms-instructions/f8880--2024.pdf` p 1 is the form, p 2 holds the
instructions and the Credit Limit Worksheet; there is no separate `i8880` for
2024). Tests are in `catala/tests/test_savers_credit.catala_en`; the oracle
comparison is `difftest/mappings/savers_credit.mjs`.

## What this module computes, and what it leaves out

- Form 8880 lines 1 to 12 for the primary filer (column (a), "You") and, on
  a joint return, the secondary filer (column (b), "Your spouse"). The output
  `qualified_saver_credit_amount` (DF `/qualifiedSaverCreditAmount`, line 12)
  feeds Schedule 3 line 4 and so Form 1040 line 20.
- Line 1 (IRA and ABLE contributions) is `$0`: DF holds it at a placeholder
  zero (`/unfilteredPrimaryFilerIraAndAbleContributions`), and a filer who
  made IRA contributions is knocked out elsewhere
  (`income.xml /madeIraContributions`). Out of scope per the issue.
- Line 2 is the W-2 box 12 elective deferrals, an input from `Form_w2s`
  (`primary_filer_total_deferrals_and_contributions`,
  `secondary_filer_total_deferrals_and_contributions`).
- Line 4 is the 1099-R distributions that count for the credit, an input from
  `Form1099_rs` (`primary_filer_savers_gross_distributions`,
  `secondary_filer_savers_gross_distributions`).
- Line 11 is the Credit Limit Worksheet. Its inputs are Form 1040 line 18
  (`total_tentative_tax`), the child and dependent care credit and the credit
  for the elderly or disabled (Schedule R). Schedule 3 lines 1, 2 (CDCC is
  line 2), 3, 6d and 6l: DF holds lines 1, 3 and 6l at `$0` placeholders
  (`schedule3.xml`), so they are not inputs here.
- The three self-reported situations that DF cannot compute (distributions in
  the last three years, distributions after the year but before the due date,
  and contributions the filer reports on his own) are knockouts
  (`ko_savers_credit_knockouts`), as in DF `flow.xml /saversCreditKnockouts`.
- Wiring (done by the orchestrator, not here): `Filers` supplies
  `is_under18` and `is_student` per filer (`FilerFacts`),
  `primary_filer_is_claimed_as_dependent`,
  `secondary_filer_is_claimed_as_dependent` and `is_mfj_dependent`;
  `Form_1040` supplies `agi` (line 11) and `total_tentative_tax` (line 18).
  The `qualified_saver_credit_amount` output feeds the Schedule 3 line 4 slot
  of the credits step; `unsupported` is part of the return's `unsupported`.

## Declarations

```catala-metadata
## The decimal amount on Form 8880 line 9. DF: saversCredits.xml
## /saversCreditMultiplierOptions.
declaration enumeration SaversCreditMultiplier:
  -- Fifty
  -- Twenty
  -- Ten
  -- Zero

## The Form 8880 lines for one person (one column of the form). Called once for
## the primary filer and once for the secondary filer.
declaration scope SaversColumn:
  # Form 8880 line 1 (IRA and ABLE contributions), already filtered by eligibility
  input line1 content money
  # Form 8880 line 2 (elective deferrals), already filtered by eligibility
  input line2 content money
  # Form 8880 line 4 (distributions)
  input line4 content money
  # Form 8880 line 3
  output line3 content money
  # Form 8880 line 5
  output line5 content money
  # Form 8880 line 6
  output line6 content money

## The whole credit.
declaration scope SaversCredit:
  # DF: filingStatus.xml /filingStatus (Writable)
  input filing_status content Types.FilingStatus
  # Form 1040 line 11. DF: taxCalculations.xml /agi
  input agi content money
  # DF: filers.xml /isMFJDependent
  input is_mfj_dependent condition
  # DF: filers.xml /primaryFiler/isUnder18
  input primary_filer_is_under18 condition
  # DF: filers.xml /primaryFiler/isStudent (Writable)
  input primary_filer_is_student condition
  # DF: filers.xml /primaryFilerIsClaimedAsDependent
  input primary_filer_is_claimed_as_dependent condition
  # DF: filers.xml /secondaryFiler/isUnder18
  input secondary_filer_is_under18 condition
  # DF: filers.xml /secondaryFiler/isStudent (Writable)
  input secondary_filer_is_student condition
  # DF: filers.xml /secondaryFilerIsClaimedAsDependent
  input secondary_filer_is_claimed_as_dependent condition
  # DF: formW2s.xml /primaryFilerW2s/*/totalDeferralsAndContributions, summed
  # (Form_w2s output primary_filer_total_deferrals_and_contributions)
  input primary_filer_total_deferrals_and_contributions content money
  # DF: formW2s.xml /secondaryFilerW2s/*/totalDeferralsAndContributions, summed
  input secondary_filer_total_deferrals_and_contributions content money
  # DF: form1099Rs.xml /primaryFiler1099RsReportedOnSaversCredit grossDistribution,
  # summed (Form1099_rs output primary_filer_savers_gross_distributions)
  input primary_filer_savers_gross_distributions content money
  # DF: form1099Rs.xml /secondaryFiler1099RsReportedOnSaversCredit, summed
  input secondary_filer_savers_gross_distributions content money
  # Form 1040 line 18. DF: taxCalculations.xml /totalTentativeTax
  input total_tentative_tax content money
  # DF: cdcc.xml /cdccTotalCredit (Schedule 3 line 2)
  input cdcc_total_credit content money
  # DF: elderlyAndDisabled.xml /totalEdc (Schedule 3 line 6d)
  input total_edc content money
  # DF: /hasDistributionsInLastThreeYears (Writable)
  input has_distributions_in_last_three_years condition
  # DF: /hasCurrentYearDistributions (Writable)
  input has_current_year_distributions condition
  # DF: /hasSelfReportedContributions (Writable)
  input has_self_reported_contributions condition

  # DF: /isFilingStatusMFJ (filingStatus.xml)
  internal is_filing_status_mfj condition
  # DF: /isFilingStatusHOH (filingStatus.xml)
  internal is_filing_status_hoh condition
  # DF: /filers/*/isEligibleForSaversCredit, primary filer
  output primary_filer_is_eligible condition
  # DF: /filers/*/isEligibleForSaversCredit, secondary filer
  output secondary_filer_is_eligible condition
  # DF: /secondaryFilerIsEligibleForSaversCredit (MFJ and secondary eligible)
  output secondary_filer_is_applicable_and_eligible condition
  # DF: /saversCreditMaxAgiLimit
  internal savers_credit_max_agi_limit content money
  # DF: /saversCreditAgiLimitForFiftyPercent
  internal savers_credit_agi_limit_for_fifty_percent content money
  # DF: /saversCreditAgiLimitForTwentyPercent
  internal savers_credit_agi_limit_for_twenty_percent content money
  # DF: /isAgiEligibleForSaversCredit
  output is_agi_eligible_for_savers_credit condition
  # DF: /eligibleForSaversCredit
  output eligible_for_savers_credit condition
  # Form 8880 lines 1a and 1b. DF: /primaryFilerIraAndAbleContributions,
  # /secondaryFilerIraAndAbleContributions
  output primary_filer_ira_and_able_contributions content money
  output secondary_filer_ira_and_able_contributions content money
  # Form 8880 lines 2a and 2b. DF: /primaryFilersDeferralsAndContributions,
  # /secondaryFilersDeferralsAndContributions
  output primary_filers_deferrals_and_contributions content money
  output secondary_filers_deferrals_and_contributions content money
  # Form 8880 lines 4a and 4b. DF: /primaryFilerGrossDistributions,
  # /secondaryFilerGrossDistributions
  output primary_filer_gross_distributions content money
  output secondary_filer_gross_distributions content money
  # The column calculations
  primary_column scope SaversColumn
  secondary_column scope SaversColumn
  # Form 8880 lines 3a and 3b. DF: /primaryFilerTotalContributions,
  # /secondaryFilerTotalContributions
  output primary_filer_total_contributions content money
  output secondary_filer_total_contributions content money
  # Form 8880 lines 5a and 5b. DF: /primaryFilerTotalContributionsLessDistributions,
  # /secondaryFilerTotalContributionsLessDistributions
  output primary_filer_total_contributions_less_distributions content money
  output secondary_filer_total_contributions_less_distributions content money
  # Form 8880 lines 6a and 6b. DF: /primaryFilerMaxCreditCalc, /secondaryFilerMaxCreditCalc
  output primary_filer_max_credit_calc content money
  output secondary_filer_max_credit_calc content money
  # Form 8880 line 7. DF: /combinedCreditLimit
  output combined_credit_limit content money
  # Form 8880 line 9. DF: /saversCreditMultiplier
  output savers_credit_multiplier content SaversCreditMultiplier
  # DF: /saversCreditMultiplierAsRational
  output savers_credit_multiplier_as_rational content decimal
  # Form 8880 line 10. DF: /ratioedCombinedCreditLimit
  output ratioed_combined_credit_limit content money
  # Form 8880 line 11. DF: /limitationBasedOnTaxLiability
  output limitation_based_on_tax_liability content money
  # DF: /qualifiedForSaverCreditWoTaxLiability
  output qualified_for_saver_credit_wo_tax_liability condition
  # DF: /qualifiedForSaverCredit
  output qualified_for_saver_credit condition
  # Form 8880 line 12. DF: /qualifiedSaverCreditAmount
  output qualified_saver_credit_amount content money
  # DF: /isReceivingSaversCredit
  output is_receiving_savers_credit condition

  # Knockout (CONVENTIONS section 6). DF: flow.xml /saversCreditKnockouts
  output ko_savers_credit_knockouts condition
  output unsupported condition
```

## Form 8880, lines 1 to 6 for one person

Form 8880 line 3: "Add lines 1 and 2". Line 5: "Subtract line 4 from line 3. If
zero or less, enter -0-". Line 6: "In each column, enter the smaller of line 5
or $2,000". (`f8880--2024.pdf` p 1)

IRC 25B(a): the credit is "the applicable percentage of so much of the
qualified retirement savings contributions of the eligible individual for the
taxable year as do not exceed $2,000." IRC 25B(d)(2)(A): the contributions
"shall be reduced (but not below zero) by the aggregate distributions received
by the individual during the testing period".

```catala
scope SaversColumn:
  # Form 8880 line 3. DF: /primaryFilerTotalContributions (Add)
  definition line3 equals line1 + line2

  # Form 8880 line 5. DF: /primaryFilerTotalContributionsLessDistributions
  # (GreaterOf(Subtract, 0))
  definition line5 equals Money.positive of (line3 - line4)

  # Form 8880 line 6, IRC 25B(a). DF: /primaryFilerMaxCreditCalc (LesserOf)
  definition line6 equals Money.min of P.savers_contribution_cap, line5
```

## Who is an eligible individual

IRC 25B(c)(1): "The term "eligible individual" means any individual if such
individual has attained the age of 18 as of the close of the taxable year."
25B(c)(2): "The term "eligible individual" shall not include— (A) any
individual with respect to whom a deduction under section 151 is allowed to
another taxpayer for a taxable year beginning in the calendar year in which
such individual's taxable year begins, and (B) any individual who is a student
(as defined in section 152(f)(2))." Form 8880 p 1: the person "(a) was born
after January 1, 2007; (b) is claimed as a dependent on someone else's 2024
tax return; or (c) was a student". The under-18 test uses the day before the
birthday (`Filers.FilerFacts.is_under18`).

Direct File: `/filers/*/isEligibleForSaversCredit` (`filers.xml` line 5311)
is the conjunction of those three tests per filer. `/eligibleForSaversCredit`
(line 212 of the module) adds "We ban an MFJ dependent here, as they have
opted not to take credits" and the AGI test.

```catala
scope SaversCredit:
  definition is_filing_status_mfj equals
    filing_status = MarriedFilingJointly
  definition is_filing_status_hoh equals
    filing_status = HeadOfHousehold

  # IRC 25B(c). DF: filers.xml /filers/*/isEligibleForSaversCredit
  definition primary_filer_is_eligible equals
    not primary_filer_is_under18
    and not primary_filer_is_claimed_as_dependent
    and not primary_filer_is_student
  definition secondary_filer_is_eligible equals
    not secondary_filer_is_under18
    and not secondary_filer_is_claimed_as_dependent
    and not secondary_filer_is_student

  # DF: /secondaryFilerIsEligibleForSaversCredit
  definition secondary_filer_is_applicable_and_eligible equals
    is_filing_status_mfj and secondary_filer_is_eligible
```

## The applicable percentage (Form 8880 line 9)

IRC 25B(b)(1): "In the case of a joint return, the applicable percentage is—
(A) if the adjusted gross income of the taxpayer is not over $30,000, 50
percent, (B) if ... over $30,000 but not over $32,500, 20 percent, (C) if ...
over $32,500 but not over $50,000, 10 percent, and (D) if ... over $50,000,
zero percent." 25B(b)(2): a head of household uses 75 percent and any other
taxpayer 50 percent of those dollar amounts, "as adjusted under paragraph
(3)". The TY2024 limits are Notice 2023-75 p 3; Form 8880 line 9 repeats them
as a table. All bounds are "not over", so AGI equal to a bound stays in the
better band (single, AGI $23,000 gives 50 percent; $23,001 gives 20 percent).

Direct File: `/saversCreditAgiLimitForFiftyPercent`,
`/saversCreditAgiLimitForTwentyPercent`, `/saversCreditMaxAgiLimit` and
`/saversCreditMultiplier`. Surviving spouses and married persons filing
separately fall in "any other taxpayer".

```catala
scope SaversCredit:
  definition savers_credit_agi_limit_for_fifty_percent equals
    if is_filing_status_mfj then P.savers_agi_limit_50_mfj
    else if is_filing_status_hoh then P.savers_agi_limit_50_hoh
    else P.savers_agi_limit_50_other

  definition savers_credit_agi_limit_for_twenty_percent equals
    if is_filing_status_mfj then P.savers_agi_limit_20_mfj
    else if is_filing_status_hoh then P.savers_agi_limit_20_hoh
    else P.savers_agi_limit_20_other

  definition savers_credit_max_agi_limit equals
    if is_filing_status_mfj then P.savers_agi_limit_10_mfj
    else if is_filing_status_hoh then P.savers_agi_limit_10_hoh
    else P.savers_agi_limit_10_other

  # DF: /isHohAgiEligibleForSaversCredit, /isMfjAgiEligibleForSaversCredit,
  # /isOtherAgiEligibleForSaversCredit, /isAgiEligibleForSaversCredit
  definition is_agi_eligible_for_savers_credit equals
    agi <= savers_credit_max_agi_limit

  # Form 8880 line 9, DF: /saversCreditMultiplier
  definition savers_credit_multiplier equals
    if agi <= savers_credit_agi_limit_for_fifty_percent then Fifty
    else if agi <= savers_credit_agi_limit_for_twenty_percent then Twenty
    else if agi <= savers_credit_max_agi_limit then Ten
    else Zero

  # DF: /saversCreditMultiplierAsRational
  definition savers_credit_multiplier_as_rational equals
    match savers_credit_multiplier with pattern
    -- Fifty : P.savers_rate_high
    -- Twenty : P.savers_rate_middle
    -- Ten : P.savers_rate_low
    -- Zero : 0%
```

## Who is eligible, and the two columns

DF `/eligibleForSaversCredit`: not an MFJ dependent; on a joint return either
filer is eligible, otherwise the primary filer; and the AGI test.

```catala
scope SaversCredit:
  # DF: /eligibleForSaversCredit
  definition eligible_for_savers_credit equals
    not is_mfj_dependent
    and (if is_filing_status_mfj
         then primary_filer_is_eligible or secondary_filer_is_eligible
         else primary_filer_is_eligible)
    and is_agi_eligible_for_savers_credit

  # Line 1. IRA and ABLE contributions are out of scope; DF holds the unfiltered
  # fact at a placeholder $0 ("Implement when we support this").
  # OUT OF SCOPE: a filer with IRA contributions is knocked out by
  # income.xml /madeIraContributions (not modelled here).
  # DF: /primaryFilerIraAndAbleContributions
  definition primary_filer_ira_and_able_contributions equals $0
  # DF: /secondaryFilerIraAndAbleContributions
  definition secondary_filer_ira_and_able_contributions equals $0

  # Line 2. DF: /primaryFilersDeferralsAndContributions rounds the sum of the
  # W-2 amounts (/unfilteredPrimaryFilersDeferralsAndContributions) and is $0
  # when the filer is not eligible.
  definition primary_filers_deferrals_and_contributions equals
    if primary_filer_is_eligible
    then R.round_dollar of primary_filer_total_deferrals_and_contributions
    else $0
  # DF: /secondaryFilersDeferralsAndContributions
  definition secondary_filers_deferrals_and_contributions equals
    if secondary_filer_is_applicable_and_eligible
    then R.round_dollar of secondary_filer_total_deferrals_and_contributions
    else $0
```

### Line 4: distributions

IRC 25B(d)(2)(A) and (B) reduce the contributions by "the aggregate
distributions received by the individual during the testing period", the
period "which includes— (i) such taxable year, (ii) the 2 preceding taxable
years, and (iii) the period after such taxable year and before the due date
(including extensions)". 25B(d)(2)(D): "any distribution received by the
spouse of such individual shall be treated as received by such individual if
such individual and spouse file a joint return for such taxable year and for
the taxable year during which the spouse receives the distribution."

Form 8880 line 4 (`f8880--2024.pdf` p 1): "If married filing jointly, include
both spouses' amounts in both columns." Instructions, p 2: "Enter the total
amount of distributions you, and your spouse if filing jointly, received after
2021 and before the due date of your 2024 return".

DF reads only the 2024 Forms 1099-R (code 2, 7, 2B, B2, 7B or B7, not a
military plan: `Form1099_rs`). The earlier years and 2025 distributions are
self-reported questions that knock the filer out (`ko_savers_credit_knockouts`),
so the 1099-R sums here are the whole of line 4 for every supported return.

DF-BUG(29-a): DF's `/primaryFilerSaversEligibleGrossDistributions` and
`/secondaryFilerSaversEligibleGrossDistributions` are `$0` unless that filer
is eligible for the credit, and `/primaryFilerGrossDistributions` and
`/secondaryFilerGrossDistributions` fall back to the filer's own (gated) sum
when that filer is not eligible. Two effects on a joint return: (1) the column
of a spouse who is a student, under 18 or claimed as a dependent shows `$0` on
line 4 (cosmetic: that column's line 2 is `$0` as well); (2) the
distributions of such a spouse drop out of line 4 of the other spouse, which
raises the credit. The statute (25B(d)(2)(D)) and the form ("include both
spouses' amounts in both columns") count the spouse's distributions whether or
not the spouse is an eligible individual. We follow them: on a joint return
both columns hold the sum of both spouses' 1099-R amounts. The oracle shows
effect (1) in two scenarios and no scenario for effect (2).
The exception on p 2 of the form (the spouses did not file jointly in the year
of the distribution) is a prior-year situation, which is a knockout.

```catala
scope SaversCredit:
  # Form 8880 line 4a. DF: /primaryFilerGrossDistributions
  # DF-BUG(29-a): DF drops an ineligible spouse's distributions; IRC
  # 25B(d)(2)(D) and the form instructions do not.
  definition primary_filer_gross_distributions equals
    if is_filing_status_mfj
    then R.round_dollar of
           (primary_filer_savers_gross_distributions
            + secondary_filer_savers_gross_distributions)
    else R.round_dollar of primary_filer_savers_gross_distributions

  # Form 8880 line 4b. DF: /secondaryFilerGrossDistributions
  definition secondary_filer_gross_distributions equals
    if is_filing_status_mfj
    then R.round_dollar of
           (primary_filer_savers_gross_distributions
            + secondary_filer_savers_gross_distributions)
    else R.round_dollar of secondary_filer_savers_gross_distributions
```

### Lines 3, 5 and 6

```catala
scope SaversCredit:
  definition primary_column.line1 equals primary_filer_ira_and_able_contributions
  definition primary_column.line2 equals primary_filers_deferrals_and_contributions
  definition primary_column.line4 equals primary_filer_gross_distributions
  definition secondary_column.line1 equals secondary_filer_ira_and_able_contributions
  definition secondary_column.line2 equals secondary_filers_deferrals_and_contributions
  definition secondary_column.line4 equals secondary_filer_gross_distributions

  definition primary_filer_total_contributions equals primary_column.line3
  definition secondary_filer_total_contributions equals secondary_column.line3
  definition primary_filer_total_contributions_less_distributions equals
    primary_column.line5
  definition secondary_filer_total_contributions_less_distributions equals
    secondary_column.line5
  definition primary_filer_max_credit_calc equals primary_column.line6
  definition secondary_filer_max_credit_calc equals secondary_column.line6

  # Form 8880 line 7: "Add the amounts on line 6". DF: /combinedCreditLimit
  definition combined_credit_limit equals
    primary_filer_max_credit_calc + secondary_filer_max_credit_calc
```

## Lines 10 to 12: the credit

Form 8880 line 10: "Multiply line 7 by line 9". DF:
`/ratioedCombinedCreditLimit` is `Round` of the multiplier times line 7
(whole dollars, ties away from zero; line 7 is whole dollars, so the product
has at most one decimal place).

Line 11 is the Credit Limit Worksheet (`f8880--2024.pdf` p 2): "1. Enter the
amount from Form 1040, 1040-SR, or 1040-NR, line 18 ... 2. Enter the total of
your credits from Schedule 3, lines 1 through 3, 6d, and 6l ... 3. Subtract
line 2 from line 1. Also enter this amount on Form 8880, line 11. But if zero
or less, stop; you can't take the credit". Line 12: "Enter the smaller of
line 10 or line 11". This is the credit order of scope.md section 6.7: CDCC
(Schedule 3 line 2) and the credit for the elderly or disabled (line 6d)
first, Saver's next.

Direct File: `/limitationBasedOnTaxLiability` subtracts
`sched3Line1 + cdccTotalCredit + sched3Line3 + totalEdc + sched3Line6l` from
`/totalTentativeTax`, with `GreaterOf(..., $0)`. The Schedule 3 lines 1, 3
and 6l are `$0` placeholders in `schedule3.xml` (foreign tax credit, education
credits and other credits, none supported), so they are omitted.

```catala
scope SaversCredit:
  # Form 8880 line 10. DF: /ratioedCombinedCreditLimit
  definition ratioed_combined_credit_limit equals
    R.round_dollar of (combined_credit_limit * savers_credit_multiplier_as_rational)

  # Form 8880 line 11, Credit Limit Worksheet. DF: /limitationBasedOnTaxLiability
  # (Schedule 3 lines 1, 3 and 6l are $0 placeholders in DF.)
  definition limitation_based_on_tax_liability equals
    Money.positive of (total_tentative_tax - (cdcc_total_credit + total_edc))

  # DF: /qualifiedForSaverCreditWoTaxLiability
  definition qualified_for_saver_credit_wo_tax_liability equals
    eligible_for_savers_credit and combined_credit_limit > $0

  # DF: /qualifiedForSaverCredit
  definition qualified_for_saver_credit equals
    qualified_for_saver_credit_wo_tax_liability
    and limitation_based_on_tax_liability > $0

  # Form 8880 line 12, limited by the Credit Limit Worksheet (line 11).
  # DF: /qualifiedSaverCreditAmount
  definition qualified_saver_credit_amount equals
    if qualified_for_saver_credit
    then Money.min of ratioed_combined_credit_limit,
                      limitation_based_on_tax_liability
    else $0

  # DF: /isReceivingSaversCredit
  definition is_receiving_savers_credit equals
    qualified_saver_credit_amount > $0
```

## Knockouts

Direct File `flow.xml` `/saversCreditKnockouts` (line 125): "Condition the
Saver's Credit knockouts on the TP qualifying for the credit": true when
`/qualifiedForSaverCredit` and any of `/hasDistributionsInLastThreeYears`,
`/hasCurrentYearDistributions` or `/hasSelfReportedContributions`. These are
the cases in which line 1 or line 4 would need data DF does not collect.
(`flow.xml` line 104 feeds this fact into `/flowIsKnockedOut`.)

```catala
scope SaversCredit:
  # DF: flow.xml /saversCreditKnockouts
  rule ko_savers_credit_knockouts under condition
    qualified_for_saver_credit
    and (has_distributions_in_last_three_years
         or has_current_year_distributions
         or has_self_reported_contributions)
  consequence fulfilled

  rule unsupported under condition ko_savers_credit_knockouts
  consequence fulfilled
```
